meta {
  name: Cancel
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/payments/{{paymentId}}/cancel
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  Admin only. UNSCHEDULED / SCHEDULED / INITIATED / FAILED -> CANCELED.
  Sets canceledAt. Cascades the linked Bill to ARCHIVED in the same
  transaction and writes `bill.archived` with
  `metadata.triggeredBy: 'payment.cancel'`. The system creates exactly
  one Payment per Bill at approve time, so a canceled Payment leaves
  the Bill with no forward motion — auto-archiving makes the dead-end
  honest in the audit trail.
}
